   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Relation between ladder rows and the paper's $\\alpha$ rows\n\nFor $L=2$, equation (E1) uses the periodic insertions $1$ and $e^{2\\pi u}$. On the three poles $u=\\theta_s-i,\\theta_s,\\theta_s+i$ of ladder $s$, the exponential is constant and equals $\\rho_s=e^{2\\pi\\theta_s}$. Hence the paper rows are a state-independent change of basis of the two ladder rows:\n\n$$N_{\\rm(E1)}=\\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\\\ \\rho_1&\\rho_2\\end{pmatrix}N_{\\rm ladder},$$\n\nup to the row normalizations $(-2\\pi)^{-\\alpha}$ and the common contour factor. Therefore\n\n$$\\det N_{\\rm(E1)}=(\\rho_2-\\rho_1)\\det N_{\\rm ladder}$$\n\n(up to those state-independent normalizations), so the two formulations are equivalent whenever $\\theta_1-\\theta_2\\notin i\\mathbb Z$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 4. Standard paper rows and a concrete norm/cross example. ---- *)\nClearAll[ρ1, ρ2, paperRowChange26, Npaper26];\npaperRowChange26 = {{1, 1}, {ρ1, ρ2}};\nNpaper26[A_, B_] := paperRowChange26 . NpaperLadder26[A, B];\nrowChangeCheck26 = And @@ Flatten[Table[\n   Together[Det[Npaper26[A, B]] - (ρ2 - ρ1) Det[NpaperLadder26[A, B]]] === 0,\n   {A, states26}, {B, states26}]];\nexampleA26 = states26[[2]];\nexampleB26 = states26[[1]];\nGrid[{\n  {\"row-change determinant identity\", rowChangeCheck26},\n  {\"norm irrep\", exampleA26[\"mu\"]},\n  {\"det N_ladder^(AA)\", Together[Det[NpaperLadder26[exampleA26, exampleA26]]]},\n  {\"cross irreps A,B\", {exampleA26[\"mu\"], exampleB26[\"mu\"]}},\n  {\"{Δt,Δc'}\", inv26[exampleA26, exampleB26]},\n  {\"N_ladder^(AB).{Δt,Δc'}\", Together[NpaperLadder26[exampleA26, exampleB26] . inv26[exampleA26, exampleB26]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
